A 3D view of Example III: the vertical slice of <m>z=\frac{x^2}{2}+\frac{y^2}{2}</m> in the direction <m>\hat{u}</m>, its tangent slope, and the level curve <m>f=1</m>.
</caption>
<interactive xml:id="interactive-gradient-max-directions-3d" iframe="gradient-max-directions-3d.html" width="100%" aspect="8:6">
<instructions>
